WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.871
agent-custody.

2
00:00:01.871 --> 00:00:04.694
Proof of what your AI agents did.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.237
Maya runs support.

4
00:00:06.237 --> 00:00:08.643
She signs a grant for her AI agent:

5
00:00:08.643 --> 00:00:10.842
refunds up to a thousand pounds,

6
00:00:10.842 --> 00:00:12.850
only for verified customers.

7
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.010
Every call goes through the gateway.

8
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.182
It checks the grant,

9
00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.881
looks the customer up itself,

10
00:00:17.881 --> 00:00:20.460
and applies the policy. Five hundred pounds?

11
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.287
Approved.

12
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.279
Then someone slips a line into a ticket,

13
00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.386
and the agent tries five thousand.

14
00:00:26.386 --> 00:00:29.227
The agent was fooled. The gateway wasn't.

15
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.290
Allowed or denied,

16
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.288
every call gets a signed receipt,

17
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:36.009
and every field says who vouches for it.

18
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.696
Its hash goes into an append-only log.

19
00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:42.750
Rewrite anything, and the root won't match.

20
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.661
Months later,

21
00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:47.634
an auditor checks it with public keys and a copy of the log.

22
00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:50.053
No login. No trust in the agent.

23
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.206
Change a single number,

24
00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:53.818
and the signature breaks.

25
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.491
Not a trace. Not a log. A receipt.

26
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.493
agent-custody.

27
00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.898
Proof of what your AI agents did.
